Z||000008||lildevil||08-19-2001||11:54 AM||||Sorry for not responding sooner. Was out of town.  The wheels are 16 inch Eagle Alloys on 225 tires in the back and 215 on the front.  And the car is lowered one inch in front and 1 1/2 in the back.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Earl_wheel.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||lildevil||08-19-2001||12:04 PM||||Doig the front facia was harder then i had originally planned and unless you have access to professional autobody bumper repair products you'll have a hard time.  I took a air hacksaw and cut along the indentation on the factory cover. Then from the piece that was cut out, cut the curved section that goes into the cover.  I then glued it into place with Sem bumper repair product.  I would FUSOR if i was to do it again. ANyways, Its important to use some kind of backing to give this supoort. I used a old damaged Fiero cover and cut pieceas off of that.  Including the gap left when cutting and moving over the curved section.  Also I had to make some metal "C" shaped brakets out of sheet metal to help hold the upper and lower sections of the opening closed. When opened up it wants to spread open. i used windshield urethan to glue the sheet metal to the cover.  The seams and such were filled with body filler.  All in all i like the way it came out...real factory looking.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/EaarlFront.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.311 @100.75 mph<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||lildevil||08-19-2001||12:12 PM||||The sail panels were done by taking the old cracked plexiglass out...be careful its sharp. And taking a grinder and grindint the area where the emblem goes to about 1/8 inch. About the same thickness as the replacment lexan.  Grind the entire surface as it will help the glues to bond and grap on to. The lexan i got from Home Depot and and cut with a fine hacksaw.  Once you have the lexan cut to shape glue it into place with windshield urethan.  Filled the seams with body filler and then plastic primed and<BR>primed hem surface and painted gloss black. <P> ||||reg||1
